Third-party files in DroidDeck's KDE desktop package (tools/desktop-kde/overlay):

- Vapor (color scheme, Plasma theme, look-and-feel package, Konsole profile and color scheme) and the
  steamdeck-gaming-return / distributor-logo-steamdeck icons: Valve's steamdeck-kde-presets
  (https://github.com/Jovian-Experiments/steamdeck-kde-presets), GPL-2.0-or-later (look-and-feel)
  and GPL-3.0 (Plasma theme), as their metadata states. The look-and-feel package's defaults, setup
  scripts and layout were adapted for DroidDeck; its Plasma 5 splash screen was left out.
- steam.svg: Papirus icon theme (https://github.com/PapirusDevelopmentTeam/papirus-icon-theme),
  GPL-3.0.

- kwin_wayland: KWin 6.8.2, GPL-2.0-or-later. Built with DroidDeck's patches in tools/desktop-kde/patches
  (nested scale, render node, scroll source and tablet input).
  Corresponding source: https://download.kde.org/stable/plasma/6.8.2/kwin-6.8.2.tar.xz and
  https://github.com/Droid-Deck/DroidDeck/tree/main/tools/desktop-kde/patches
  (the source and the hashes of the applied patches are recorded in desktop-kde.kwin.txt beside the package).

Everything else in the package is Arch Linux ARM's own packages, under their own licenses
(/usr/share/licenses).
